    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the \"unintended consequences\" bit is pretty vague tho. if you look at the actual data from places that tried it in Europe, doesn't it pretty much prove that capital flight is the bigger risk? like, it seems like the inequality argument is more of a theoretical ideal while the investment side is just how markets actually work.",
